        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.492,
            0.9,
            0.531
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "13.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A die is thrown once. Find the probability of getting (i) a prime number; (ii) a number lying between 2 and 6; (iii) an odd number."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.535,
            0.899,
            0.594
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "14.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " One card is drawn from a well-shuffled deck of 52 cards. Find the probability of getting (i) a king of red colour (ii) a face card (iii) a red face card (iv) the jack of hearts (v) a spade (vi) the queen of diamonds"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.115,
            0.599,
            0.901,
            0.634
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "15.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " Five cards—the ten, jack, queen, king and ace of diamonds, are well-shuffled with their face downwards. One card is then picked up at random."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.171,
            0.637,
            0.645,
            0.656
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What is the probability that the card is the queen?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.165,
            0.658,
            0.9,
            0.694
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) If the queen is drawn and put aside, what is the probability that the second card picked up is (a) an ace? (b) a queen?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.698,
            0.901,
            0.753
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "16.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " 12 defective pens are accidentally mixed with 132 good ones. It is not possible to just look at a pen and tell whether or not it is defective. One pen is taken out at random from this lot. Determine the probability that the pen taken out is a good one."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.757,
            0.899,
            0.792
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "17.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " (i) A lot of 20 bulbs contain 4 defective ones. One bulb is drawn at random from the lot. What is the probability that this bulb is defective?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 16,
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.795,
            0.902,
            0.847
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) Suppose the bulb drawn in (i) is not defective and is not replaced. Now one bulb is drawn at random from the rest. What is the probability that this bulb is not defective ?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 17,
          "bbox": [
            0.114,
            0.853,
            0.902,
            0.907
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "18.",
              "styles": [
                "bold"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": " A box contains 90 discs which are numbered from 1 to 90. If one disc is drawn at random from the box, find the probability that it bears (i) a two-digit number (ii) a perfect square number (iii) a number divisible by 5."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
